e main diagonal are the same, while the antidiagonal entries have opposite signs.\n\nWith that in mind let's check each of the given matrices:\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is *not* a rotation-scaling matrix since the entries on the antidiagonal do not have opposite signs.\n\n- $B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ is a rotation-scaling matrix.\n\n- $C=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -8\\end{aligned}]$ is *not* a rotation-scaling matrix since the entries on the main diagonal are not the same.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81453/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "359bc41e-1b6d-5177-9642-4f8697bc5ba0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81453"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140397/selection/ce5b3907bb169edb7e2da6fd6b2f283b2d531922ca9709f0e6ddae15080c9b52" :answer/id #uuid "92e6f317-ee6b-547a-944c-e0fefbdcdfef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140397/selection/e7412ea6d90edda6b9055dee863f96c25ea7817347f157e928d200430c4a4de4" :answer/id #uuid "7c41c2af-17fa-5d4a-bef1-538aa89becc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140397/selection/b8c8a17d726025b4818fa0948673ccb32061775ca68a482b545be0287f5dc0d3" :answer/id #uuid "685cf9e8-78d6-57f3-997c-f6e8874ac4f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140397/selection/108a7cb90749958e3fcab4a49793145d8130c76886e2904a5854edc1f5c78191" :answer/id #uuid "86457889-26f9-55e9-8eca-235